{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1795313076,"nonce":"Ay7Iki1/Ek2NsYdTogF/Tjd98/Q=","message":"Step 3 is done in 917f891f. A wait in the runtime or in a plugin no longer holds up a collection when ZYNTAX_IMMIX_THREADS=1.\n\nThe design changed in one place. The SDK hook is one callback, not an enter and leave pair. zrtl::heap::set_blocking(run, poll) takes a function that runs a closure inside the host's blocking region, and a function that polls the stop flag. The host spills the registers and publishes the roots in its own frame, and that frame lives for the whole wait. The SDK wraps a Rust closure in a trampoline and passes a panic through. A plugin loaded from a library gets the hooks through a new _zrtl_set_blocking export. The embed runtime installs them next to the allocator.\n\nAnnotated, each inside blocking: thread join, park, channel recv and the two recv_timeout calls, contended mutex_lock, the global map locks of the thread plugin, the four time sleeps, the band pool's idle worker wait and dispatcher wait, the promise timer sleep and the three host future sleeps. Polling the safepoint: atomic_load, atomic_compare_exchange, thread_yield_now, the promise wait loops and the six spin loops of the SDK's async support.\n\nTests. The Immix unit test for a polling thread fails when safepoint does nothing. A new integration test, band_pool_collect, runs four pool threads that each keep a list and allocate garbage, while the dispatcher keeps its own list, at a 256 KB floor. Every list survives, collections run, and no stop is cancelled. It fails when the idle worker's wait or the dispatcher's wait is not in a region. It passed 60 runs in a row. The SDK and the thread plugin each test that their waits go through the hook.\n\nReal programs, Mac release build, flag on: Python conformance 50 of 50, Lua conformance 46 of 46 and official_suite 4 of 4, with no cancelled stop in the logs. Band pool dispatch costs the same with the flag on or off within noise: 7 to 13 us at best in both arms. The worst case was 1 to 3 us higher with the flag on.\n\nNot done. sdl_delay and window_delay still sleep outside a region, because this Mac has no SDL to build them. Idle pool workers now register at their first wait, so each one publishes roots on every wait. A mutex_lock that is held for ever and a receive that holds a global lock are separate faults, filed as 68a13d7.\n\nStep 4 is next. Thread start-up arguments, closure environments moved into a spawned thread, channel payloads, thread results and promise values sit where no collection reads. A thread that receives a pointer must also be registered before it holds the pointer, or its stack is never scanned.","files":null}]}